# MoE host CPU compute tier VENICE: census-seeded static partition (patch 0046)

# Applied on top of patches/0003-0045, against the pinned runtime build
# 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29. Mechanism (campaign docs/campaigns/expert-hot-
# set-lru.md, design docs/design-expert-hot-set-lru.md Section 5.1): patch
# 0018 chooses a layer's resident expert set with a frequency-FREE
# splitmix64(seed, layer_key, expert) rank, measured (tools/
# expert_policy_compare.py) to sit at CHANCE at every budget (0.92-1.10x
# slots/512). VENICE replaces that ranking with a measured-frequency rank
# from a served-routing census, so the pinned half is the hot half.
#
# Where it lives:
#   src/plugins/intel_gpu/src/graph/impls/ocl_v2/moe/census_seed.hpp  (new)
#     a dependency-free parser for the "hot-set seed v2" format, one line per
#     layer `<layer_key> <expert> <expert> ...`, with a MANDATORY
#     `# space=layer_key` header. Malformed lines, duplicate layer_keys,
#     duplicate expert ids, a missing/wrong space header and an empty file are
#     REFUSED (std::runtime_error), not defaulted.
#     census_seed_resident_experts() validates one layer against the model:
#     the layer_key must be present, the expert count must equal the pool
#     capacity (a budget that moved since the census is a mismatch), and every
#     expert id must be < num_expert.
#   .../expert_weight_providers.hpp/.cpp
#     OffloadExpertWeightProvider gains set_census_seed()/census_seed_active()
#     and bind() pins the census set when active, else patch 0018's splitmix64
#     rank. Both are pure functions of the layer's recorded inputs, so DESIGN
#     Section 3.4 (history-independent greedy output) is untouched.
#   .../moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp
#     the impl constructor reads the per-run env var MOE_CPU_TIER_SEED (a path)
#     once per process (cached across the 48 layers), validates this layer's
#     entry at construction -- so a mismatched seed REFUSES THE LOAD before any
#     request is served -- and logs `seed_source=census|census_seed_fp=0x...`
#     beside the existing seed/resident_checksum fields. Unset env = patch
#     0018 behaviour, byte-for-byte.
#
# Invariant: the seed is a pure function of the RECORDED census (the corpus
# census, tools/hot_set_census.py select --census), not of run history, so
# DESIGN Section 3.4 still holds. The seed does not change the arithmetic a
# non-resident expert runs: residency only decides WHICH arithmetic (device
# f16 vs host f32) an expert takes, and patch 0018 makes that set history-free.
#
# Evidence class: this header is `code`. Its device-free refusal cells are in
# tools/test_census_seed.py (compile the header with g++ and exercise each
# malformed/mismatched case). The served quality row is measured on the A770.
